body:
### Is it platform specific

generic

### Importance or Severity

Low

### Description of the enhancement

Add yang model support to set loopback interface as sflow agent id. CLI support already exists for the same.


### Current Behavior

CLI support to set loopback interface as sflow agent id is already supported. However setting teh same using GCU fails due to yang model validation.

### Proposed Behavior

Should be able to set loopback interface as flow agent id as described below:

admin$ jsondiff empty.json sflow.json | jq
[
  {
    "op": "add",
    "path": "/SFLOW",
    "value": {
      "global": {
        "admin_state": "up",
        "agent_id": "Loopback1"
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "op": "add",
    "path": "/SFLOW_COLLECTOR",
    "value": {
      "sp1.58": {
        "collector_ip": "200.1.1.204",
        "collector_port": "6343",
        "collector_vrf": "default"
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "op": "add",
    "path": "/SFLOW_SESSION",
    "value": {
      "Ethernet480": {
        "admin_state": "up",
        "sample_direction": "rx",
        "sample_rate": "131072"
      }
    }
  }
]
jsondiff empty.json sflow.json | sudo config apply-patch /dev/stdin
